			"notes": "# Initial release of CmdTree\n\n## Download\n\nGrab the **regular** jar matching your Minecraft version below. Don't download the `-sources.jar` files, those are just the Java source for reference/debugging and won't work as a mod. You'll also need [Fabric Loader](https://fabricmc.net/use/) and a matching build of [Fabric API](https://modrinth.com/mod/fabric-api) installed. \n\n| Minecraft | Jar |\n|---|---|\n| 1.20.1 | `cmdtree-1.0.0+1.20.1.jar` |\n| 1.20.4 | `cmdtree-1.0.0+1.20.4.jar` |\n| 1.21.1 | `cmdtree-1.0.0+1.21.1.jar` |\n| 1.21.4 | `cmdtree-1.0.0+1.21.4.jar` |\n| 1.21.8 | `cmdtree-1.0.0+1.21.8.jar` |\n| 1.21.11 | `cmdtree-1.0.0+1.21.11.jar` |\n| 26.1.2 | `cmdtree-1.0.0+26.1.2.jar` |\n| 26.2 | `cmdtree-1.0.0+26.2.jar` |\n\n## Notes\n\n- If another installed mod registers a custom Brigadier argument type that vanilla doesn't recognize (seen with older builds of GMDetector), CmdTree now falls back to a reduced description for just that command instead of failing the whole dump.\n\nSee the [README](https://github.com/AlexWeber64/cmdtree#readme) for full usage details."
